# Paradigm - agentic-commerce

> **Author:** Matt Canoy ([@ascend42](https://github.com/ascend42)) | **Repo:** [github.com/ascend42/a-paradigm](https://github.com/ascend42/a-paradigm) | **npm:** [@a-company/paradigm](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@a-company/paradigm)

## CRITICAL RULES (Non-Negotiable)

1. **You MUST update the nearest `.purpose` file when you change behavior.** No exceptions.
2. **You MUST call `paradigm_session_recover` at session start and `paradigm_pm_postflight` when finishing.** See `paradigm-workflow.mdc` for the full protocol.
3. **You MUST call `paradigm_ripple` before modifying any documented symbol.** Check impact before changing code.

Violating these rules means your changes are non-compliant. The `paradigm-workflow.mdc` file contains the complete workflow — follow it.

## Overview

This project uses Paradigm for structured AI-assisted development.
All context, symbols, and specifications live in the .paradigm/ directory.


## How to Use Paradigm

- Check .paradigm/specs/ for philosophy and patterns before making changes
- Reference symbols using prefixes: #component ^gate !signal $flow ~aspect
- Use the Paradigm logger instead of raw console.log/print statements
- Run `paradigm probe` with screenshots to map UI to code
- Check .paradigm/docs/ for command reference and troubleshooting
- Read .index.yaml files first when navigating documentation
- Use `paradigm team handoff` when approaching context limits


## When to Update Paradigm Files

- When adding a feature, create/update the nearest .purpose file
- When adding authorization, update portal.yaml
- When exploring ideas, use [idea] tag on any symbol
- Always update references when renaming symbols
